cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "WildfireGuardian"
abstract: >-
  Wildfire spread forecasting turned into household-level evacuation routing and
  rescue dispatch for rural elderly residents in Korea. Every figure the project
  states in prose is registered in docs/NUMBERS.json and re-derived from a
  committed artifact by `make verify`.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Park"
    given-names: "Siyeong"
    alias: "박시영"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sparkxt-0318/wildfireguardian"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0-alpha"
keywords:
  - wildfire
  - evacuation routing
  - time-dependent shortest path
  - emergency response
  - OpenStreetMap
# No `doi:` and no `date-released:` field: no release has been tagged and no DOI has
# been minted. Both are the author's to do from a browser session after the finals
# (WFG-031), and a fabricated release date is exactly the kind of figure this
# repository refuses to write.
